# Frontend: GNOME (Wayland, mutter/gnome-shell), for desktop x86_64/arm64
# machines. IN PROGRESS - this fragment still deliberately sets nothing; a
# board including it fails loudly at review rather than half-building a
# desktop. What changed since the placeholder: the dependency audit below
# is done, and the stage-1 packages exist in external/.
#
# The plan, verified against this Buildroot tree (systemd-free GNOME the
# way Gentoo/Alpine ship it - elogind on OpenRC):
#
#   Already in Buildroot: polkit, upower, network-manager, libsecret, gcr,
#   libsoup3, libical, json-glib, graphene, pipewire, libdisplay-info,
#   gstreamer1, libgudev, gsettings-desktop-schemas, adwaita-icon-theme.
#
#   Stage 1 (DONE, external/): elogind - the org.freedesktop.login1
#       provider mutter/gnome-shell hard-require; dconf - the GSettings
#       backend; libnotify.
#   Stage 2 (DONE, external/): gtk4 (wayland+x11 backends), libadwaita,
#       and the appstream it links against.
#   Stage 3: mozjs (SpiderMonkey; needs the rust host-toolchain - the
#       single hardest cross-compile in the stack) and gjs on top of it.
#   Stage 4: libei, mutter (Wayland-native: no X server needed),
#       gnome-settings-daemon (colord/geocode/libgweather integrations
#       off), gnome-session; wire PAM + pam_elogind into login - without
#       it elogind registers no sessions and the compositor cannot start.
#   Stage 5: evolution-data-server (a gnome-shell hard dependency;
#       libical/libsecret/libsoup3 are present), gnome-shell, and an
#       xdg-desktop-portal set. No gdm: the tty1 autologin dispatch
#       starts the session, like the sway and XFCE frontends.
#
# Nautilus/gnome-control-center and friends come after the shell runs.
